      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mears was founded in 1873 by mill owner Charles Mears, who also opened the town’s first post office that same month.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mears%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Silver Lake Sand Dunes, the town’s signature landmark, draw over a million visitors each year to its towering dunes and pristine beaches.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mears%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mears sits on Michigan’s Lower Peninsula, just 3 miles west of Hart and 39 miles north of Muskegon, offering easy access to the Great Lakes coast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mears%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Oceana County Historical Park in Mears now houses five historic buildings and a storage facility, preserving the area’s early 20th‑century heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://thinkdunes.com/business/oceana-county-historical-genealogical-society/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The park’s collection includes the historic Swedish Mission Church, a rare example of 19th‑century Scandinavian ecclesiastical architecture in Michigan.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://thinkdunes.com/business/oceana-county-historical-genealogical-society/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Local volunteers run guided tours of the museum, sharing stories of Oceana County’s past and hosting community fundraisers to support preservation efforts.",
